.TH FATRAT-TUI 1 "October 17, 2026"
.SH NAME
fatrat-tui \- terminal client for the FatRat download manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fatrat-tui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfatrat-tui\fP is a full-screen terminal (ncurses) client for
.BR fatrat (1).
It manages transfers and queues, shows transfer details, the RSS feeds and
rules, the log, the settings, the scheduler and the Python extensions.
It talks to FatRat over its REST API; it needs a terminal and a FatRat built
with the web interface.
.PP
By default (\fB\-\-mode auto\fR) it uses, in this order:
a server that is already running on the unix socket;
a running FatRat on this machine whose settings turn on the web interface;
or a private server that it starts itself on the unix socket.
Use \fB\-\-which\fR to see what it would do.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.B \-\-mode \fImode\fR
How to reach FatRat: \fBauto\fR (the default); \fBlocal\fR, the running FatRat
found through its settings; \fBsocket\fR, a server on the unix socket, started
if needed; or \fBurl\fR (needs \fB\-\-url\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-url \fIurl\fR
Connect to a FatRat web interface: \fIhttp://host:port\fR,
\fIhttps://host:port\fR or \fIunix:/path/to.sock\fR. Implies \fB\-\-mode url\fR.
May also be given in the \fBFATRAT_URL\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-start
In auto mode, do not start a server; fail if none is running.
.TP
.B \-\-which
Print how \fBfatrat-tui\fR would connect, and why, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file \fIfile\fR
Read the web interface password from the first line of \fIfile\fR. The file
must not be accessible by group or others.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-prompt
Ask for the password even if \fBFATRAT_PASSWORD\fR, \fB\-\-password\-file\fR or
the settings of a local FatRat provide one.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Do not verify the server certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIpath\fR
Unix socket of the local server (default:
\fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fatrat/rest.sock\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-server\-bin \fIpath\fR
The FatRat program to start (default: \fBfatrat-nogui\fR or \fBfatrat\fR next
to this program, or in \fBPATH\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIfile\fR
FatRat settings file: read to find a running FatRat, and used by a server that
\fBfatrat-tui\fR starts (default: the normal FatRat settings).
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop a local server that was started by \fBfatrat-tui\fR, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Do not use the mouse.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Draw with plain ASCII characters.
.TP
.B \-\-script \fIfile\fR
Run the commands in \fIfile\fR against a virtual screen and print the results.
Meant for tests.
.TP
.B \-\-size \fIcolsxrows\fR
Screen size for \fB\-\-script\fR (default 110x34).
.SH KEYS
Keys act on the focused pane; the bottom bar always shows those that apply.
Press \fB?\fR or \fBF1\fR for the full list.
Letters are plain keys (not Ctrl combinations) and may be upper or lower case.
.SS Everywhere
.TP
.B 1, 2, 3
Switch to Transfers, RSS or Log.
.TP
.B F2 (O), F4 (X)
Settings, extensions.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift\-Tab
Move focus between panes (next tab in the details view).
.TP
.B Up (K), Down (J), PgUp, PgDn, Home, End
Move through a list.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Focus the queues or the transfers pane (in a narrow terminal: previous and
next queue).
.TP
.B /
Filter the transfers by name (search, in the log).
.TP
.B Esc
Go back or close a dialog; on the Transfers tab, clear the filter, then the
marks.
.TP
.B ? (F1)
Help.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B Q, Ctrl\-C
Quit. If \fBfatrat-tui\fR started the private server itself, the server is
stopped too; when transfers are active, it first asks whether to keep the
server running or stop it. If \fBfatrat-tui\fR is ended by \fBSIGTERM\fR,
\fBSIGHUP\fR or a lost terminal, it does not ask: it stops the server only if
nothing is active.
A server that was already running is never stopped.
.SS Transfers
.TP
.B R, F, P
Resume, force-start and pause the selected transfers. Resume turns a forced
transfer into a normal one and queues paused and failed ones.
.TP
.B N, E, D
New transfer, edit its properties, delete.
.TP
.B M, [, ]
Move: \fBM\fR then \fBT\fR (top), \fBU\fR (up), \fBD\fR (down) or \fBB\fR
(bottom); or \fB[\fR and \fB]\fR to move up and down.
.TP
.B S, L
Send to another queue; speed limit.
.TP
.B Space, A
Mark or unmark a transfer; mark all or none.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the details of a transfer.
.SS Queues
.TP
.B N, E, D
New, edit and delete a queue.
.TP
.B [, ]
Move the queue up or down.
.TP
.B L, Enter
Queue speed limits; open the queue.
.SS Details and torrent files
.TP
.B Tab, Shift\-Tab
Next and previous tab.
.TP
.B Esc, B
Back to the list.
.TP
.B + (=), \-, S, A, Enter
Torrent files: raise or lower the priority, skip a file, download all files,
apply the changes.
.SS RSS and log
.TP
.B N, E, D, R, Tab
RSS: new, edit, delete, refresh the feeds now, switch between feeds and rules.
.TP
.B T, W
RSS rules: test a regular expression; the downloaded episodes.
.TP
.B F, /, N, G, End, T
Log: follow the end, search, next match, top, bottom, log of the selected
transfer (or back to the global log).
.SS In dialogs
.TP
.B Tab, Shift\-Tab, Up, Down
Next and previous field.
.TP
.B Space
Tick a check box or change a choice.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-A, Ctrl\-E, Ctrl\-U, Ctrl\-K, Ctrl\-W
Start of the text, end of the text, clear the field, delete to the end, delete
the word before the cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-B
Browse for a directory.
.TP
.B Enter, Esc
Save, cancel.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FATRAT_URL
Default for \fB\-\-url\fR.
.TP
.B FATRAT_PASSWORD
The web interface password, used for connections over the network.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the default unix socket lives.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fatrat/tui.conf
Settings of \fBfatrat-tui\fR, including trusted server certificate fingerprints.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fatrat/rest.sock
Default unix socket of the local server.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
if the connection plan failed under \fB\-\-which\fR, no terminal is available, or
\fB\-\-stop\fR found nothing to stop; \fB2\fR for invalid options or a connection
that cannot be planned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fatrat (1)
.PP
